'''Grup Ciutat Nova''' ({{lang|ca|Grup Ciutat Nova}}; "New City Group") is a [[Balboa|Balboan]] real estate development company and the largest property developer in the country. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and is a component of the [[SCX 30]] index. The company is best known for its shopping centres, residential high-rises, and mixed-use developments in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and the other major cities of the [[Estret Province|Estret]] corridor.

== History ==

=== Founding ===

Grup Ciutat Nova was founded in 1993 by [[Ricard Soler i Vidal]], a construction contractor from [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], during the sustained suburban boom that followed reunification. The outer ciutats of Sant Cristòfor — Sant Jordi, Sant Martí, Sant Llorenç, Ciutat de l'Estació — were growing rapidly as families moved out of the historic core, and the satellite cities of the [[Estret Province|Estret]] corridor were expanding to accommodate the canal corridor's growing workforce. At the same time, Dàrsena was being deindustrialised — the steel mill had closed in 1982, the chemical plant in 1987, and the last major facilities had shut down by the early 1990s — creating a secondary market for urban regeneration.

The company's early business was built on suburban residential development: new housing estates and apartment blocks in the expanding outer ciutats and the towns along the Estret corridor between Sant Cristòfor and [[Portnou]]. These projects provided the steady cash flow and land bank that allowed the company to grow. The company also undertook some of the early warehouse conversions in Dàrsena — loft apartments and commercial spaces marketed to artists and young professionals — but these were a smaller part of its portfolio during the 1990s.

=== Urban renaissance ===

The turn of the millennium marked a shift in the company's focus. The urban renaissance of 2000–2015 saw young professionals and the growing middle class returning to the city core, drawn by the cultural life of Dàrsena and the improving infrastructure of Original. Grup Ciutat Nova moved aggressively into new-build development: shopping centres in the growing residential districts, and high-rise apartment towers along the Sant Cristòfor waterfront and in the regenerated docklands areas.

The company's shopping centres became anchors for new residential districts, creating the mixed-use neighbourhoods that defined Sant Cristòfor's expansion in the 2000s and 2010s. The residential towers — marketed to young professionals, returning residents, and foreign investors — were among the first modern high-rises in the city and set the architectural tone for the waterfront skyline.

In the 2010s, Grup Ciutat Nova expanded to other Balboan cities, undertaking developments in [[Portnou]], [[Sant Llàtzer]], and the provincial capitals. The company also began developing office towers in El Centre, responding to demand from the financial services sector and the canal corridor's growing corporate presence.

== Portfolio ==

=== Shopping centres ===

Grup Ciutat Nova is the largest operator of shopping centres in Balboa. Its properties are concentrated in the Estret corridor and serve as commercial anchors for the residential districts the company develops. The company's shopping centres typically include anchor department stores, multiplex cinemas, food courts, and multilevel parking, and are designed to function as suburban town centres for the residential areas that surround them.

=== Residential high-rises ===

The company's residential division constructs high-rise apartment towers in Sant Cristòfor and other Estret cities. Developments range from luxury waterfront apartments to mid-market towers in regenerated neighbourhoods. The company's residential projects have been a major driver of the return-to-city trend in Sant Cristòfor, providing the modern housing stock that the city's older building stock could not offer.

=== Mixed-use and office ===

Grup Ciutat Nova's mixed-use developments combine retail, residential, and office space in single projects, typically in El Centre or along the waterfront. The company has also developed several purpose-built office towers in the financial district, leasing space to banks, law firms, and canal corridor service companies.

